l 1 % de todos sus contratos de obras. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 39 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 39.421,49 euros, se adjudicó en noviembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El hecho de que se adjudiquen contratos al límite no implica que haya sido un error. Puede deberse a razones legales o a necesidades específicas.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros años. Analizar si los contratos al límite se distribuyen por necesidades distintas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 65 minor contracts for works above 37,500 and up to 40,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 4.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 14.8, with a 95% confidence interval of 9.0 to 25.2. December accounts for 0% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 1% of all its works contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 6. Contract [1], for 39,421.49 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove misconduct. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate improper actions by any party.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contract details for [1] to see what was purchased and the exact date. Review awardee A’s contracts to identify if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Look for repeated purchases to determine if needs were prioritized over cost efficiency.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["1BqnZ3COxZqGCFcHcNGIlQ%3D%3D","xwWHTBxPn3eHCIsjvJ3rhQ%3D%3D","o8mdE7f6HSGP%2Bo96UAV7cQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}